  "raw_html": "<button type='button' role='link' class='btn btn-link p-0 text-start' id='link_5' aria-label=\" The State of Kerala  versus M. Vijayakumar & Ors. pdf\"  class='noToken' href='#' onclick=javascript:open_pdf('5','2026','2026_5_119_134','2026INSC352'); ><font size='4'> <strong>THE STATE OF KERALA <span class='fst-italic'> versus </span>M. VIJAYAKUMAR & ORS. </strong>- <span class='escrText'>[2026] 5 S.C.R. 119</span><span class='ncDisplay'>2026 INSC 352</span><input type='hidden' id='cnr' value=ESCR010001372026></button></font><br><strong>Coram : MANOJ MISRA<sup style=\"color: #268e97;font-size: 22px;top: 0;\" class=\"tooltip-sup\" data-tooltip=\"Author\">*</sup>, PRASANNA BHALACHANDRA VARALE</strong><br> Issue for Consideration If Dearness Allowance (DA) and Dearness Relief (DR) are to be added on salary and pension payable to serving employees and retired employees, respectively, whether there could be a higher rate for enhancement of DA than what it is for DR. Headnotes&dagger; Constitution of Dearness Allowance and Dearness Relief &ndash; Retired employees of KSRTC filed a writ petition questioning the lower rate fixed for enhancement of DR on pension than what was fixed for enhancement of DA on salary &ndash; Their grievance was that the serving employees got enhancement of DA by 14<br><strong class='caseDetailsTD' ><span style='color:#212F3D' > Decision Date :</span><font color='green'> 10-04-2026</font><span style='color:#212F3D' > | Case No :</span><font color='green'> CIVIL APPEAL No. 4347/2026</font><span style='color:#212F3D' > | Disposal Nature :</span><font color='green'> Dismissed</font>   <span style='color:#212F3D' > |  Bench :</span><font color='green'> 2 Judges</font></strong><div class='row my-1 mt-2 border bg-light'><div class='col-auto'><a href='#' class='btn btn-outline-secondary btn-sm my-1' onclick=open_splitview('5','2026','2026_5_119_134','2026INSC352','S')><i <i class='fas fa-columns me-2'></i>Split view</a></div><div class='co